<title>USA: Indianapolis to weigh new arena for Pacers.</title>
<headline>Indianapolis to weigh new arena for Pacers.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indianapolis' city-county council will hear reports next week on building a new arena for the Indiana Pacers basketball team, a spokesman for Mayor Stephen Goldsmith said Monday.</p>
<p>Ed Sagebiel said a capital improvement board charged by Goldsmith to study the stadium issue will present its findings at the Dec. 16 council meeting. Those findings will include financing mechanisms for a $150 million to $175 million arena and site locations, he added.</p>
<p>Sagebiel said the council will also hear from Pacers representatives.</p>
<p>The Pacers currently play in Market Square Arena, which was built in 1974.</p>
<p>--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
